There probably have been many before me complaining about this, but I
will write about it anyway.

Something that bothers me about Nethack's score system is that when
going for pacifist (which I usually do) most of your score (if you are
a successful pacifist) is decided by how deep your deepest level was. I
think this deepest level doesn't mean much in a game where you actually
ascend.

For pacifists the things that should matter are:
- Did you engrave that wand to id it (getting 10 score) or did you
refrain from it.
- Did you use oracle to get to lvl 3 easily or did you not
- etc

The difference in score should be in those details.

Would it be difficult (and supported) to change the code that when you
ascend you don't get ant score for levels reached deeper that the
highest possible place where Inner sanctum can be? So effectively (as
fas as score is concerned) everyone's inner sanctum was just as deep.

